# Linux Security with SELinux and AppArmor

## Course Overview

Linux is widely used in enterprise environments to host critical applications and sensitive data. Protecting these systems requires more than traditional Linux file permissions. This course introduces **Security-Enhanced Linux (SELinux)** and **AppArmor**, two powerful Mandatory Access Control (MAC) frameworks that provide an additional layer of security by controlling how users, processes, and applications interact with system resources.

The course begins with the fundamentals of SELinux, including its architecture, operating modes, security contexts, and resource labeling. Learners will then install and configure SELinux on Ubuntu Linux, manage SELinux users and security contexts, secure Apache Web Server resources, and troubleshoot common access control issues. Finally, the course introduces AppArmor, explains its profile-based security model, and compares it with SELinux.

This course is designed for Linux administrators, security engineers, DevOps professionals, and anyone preparing for the **CompTIA Linux+ (XK0-005)** certification.

