# Module 3: Installing SELinux on Ubuntu

Unlike Red Hat-based distributions, Ubuntu requires SELinux packages to be installed manually.

### Installation Steps

* Stop AppArmor service.
* Disable AppArmor.
* Update package repositories.
* Install SELinux packages.
* Activate SELinux.
* Reboot the system.
* Verify installation.

### Commands

```bash
sudo service apparmor stop
sudo systemctl disable apparmor

sudo apt update

sudo apt install policycoreutils \
selinux-utils \
selinux-basics

sudo selinux-activate

sudo init 6

sudo sestatus
sudo getenforce
```

### Configuration File

```
/etc/selinux/config
```

Important configuration:

```
SELINUX=permissive
SELINUX=enforcing
SELINUX=disabled
```

