# Module 8: AppArmor Fundamentals

AppArmor is another Linux Mandatory Access Control framework used primarily by Ubuntu and SUSE Linux.

Unlike SELinux, AppArmor secures applications using security profiles.

### AppArmor Modes

### Complain Mode

* Monitors activity
* Logs violations
* Does not block access

### Enforce Mode

* Enforces policies
* Blocks unauthorized access
* Recommended for production

### Commands

```bash
apparmor_status

aa-enforce

aa-complain

systemctl disable apparmor
```

### Practical Activities

* View loaded profiles.
* Switch profiles to Enforce mode.
* Switch profiles to Complain mode.
* Configure application profiles.
* Protect custom applications.

---

# SELinux vs AppArmor

| Feature             | SELinux              | AppArmor             |
| ------------------- | -------------------- | -------------------- |
| Security Model      | Label-Based          | Profile-Based        |
| Configuration       | Complex              | Simpler              |
| Flexibility         | Very High            | Moderate             |
| Default Platforms   | RHEL, CentOS, Fedora | Ubuntu, SUSE         |
| Policy Management   | Security Contexts    | Application Profiles |
| Enterprise Adoption | Very High            | High                 |

